title: Analytics › Common denial reasons: open Denial Intelligence
route: /analytics
intro: The table of common denial reasons. Every row is a link to Denial Intelligence, by the row or by the reason text. The link opens the plain denial list. It does not carry the payer or the reason across.
dir: TD
---
start s1 "Scroll to 'Common denial reasons by payer'"
screen sc "Card 'Common denial reasons by payer'\n'This quarter · 311 denials in the reasons listed. Select a row to open Denial Intelligence.'"
screen th "Columns\n'Reason', 'Payer', 'Count', 'Share of denials' (a red bar and the percent)"

decision q1 "Which payer is chosen in the menu?"
process p1 "'All payers': one row per payer, its most common reason\nBiggest first"
screen r1 "Cardinal 89 · 29%\n'Continued-stay evidence incomplete'"
screen r2 "Harborview MA 74 · 24%\n'Recertification filed too late'"
screen r3 "Evergreen 61 · 20%\n'Partial approval without a stated reason'"
screen r4 "Summit Medicaid 48 · 15%\nBeacon PPO 39 · 13%"
process p2 "A payer with fewer than 20 listed denials is left out\nLakeshore this quarter and last quarter"
process p3 "One payer: all of that payer's reasons, three or four rows\nShares add up to 100% of the listed denials"
decision q2 "Fewer than 20 denials listed?"
screen nd "'Not enough decisions yet. Figures based on fewer than 20 decisions stay hidden.'\nNo table, no link"

group gClick "Open a row"
  click c1 "Click anywhere on a row"
  click c2 "Click the reason text, for example 'Recertification filed too late'"
  process p4 "Opens /denials with no payer or reason chosen\nRow hover tint shows it is a link"
endgroup

goto g1 "Continues in: Denial Intelligence › Open denials list"
process p5 "Browser Back returns to Analytics with the menus reset"

s1 --> sc --> th --> q1
q1 -->|All payers| p1
p1 --> r1 & r2 & r3 & r4
p1 -.-> p2
q1 -->|One payer| p3
p3 --> q2
p2 --> q2
q2 -->|Yes| nd
q2 -->|No| c1 & c2
r1 & r2 & r3 & r4 --> c1 & c2
c1 --> p4
c2 --> p4
p4 --> g1
g1 -.-> p5
